<div class="min-h-screen">
  <header class="grid border-b border-black lg:grid-cols-2">
    <div class="flex flex-col justify-center gap-8 bg-pink px-8 py-16 text-black lg:px-16 lg:py-24">
      <p class="text-xl">Sell digital products with AI</p>
      <h1 class="text-5xl font-medium leading-none text-balance sm:text-6xl xl:text-7xl">Gumroad MCP</h1>
      <p class="max-w-xl text-xl sm:text-2xl">Connect your Gumroad store to the AI assistant you already use. Check sales, draft products, publish them, and track payouts from your chat.</p>
      <div class="flex flex-col items-start gap-5">
        <%= render "home/shared/button", text: "Set up the connector", url: "#connect", variant: "dark" %>
        <p class="text-base">You’ll need a Gumroad account and an assistant that supports MCP.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="hidden items-center justify-center border-l border-black bg-yellow px-12 py-12 text-black lg:flex">
      <%= image_tag "mcp/creator.svg", alt: "A smiling Gumroad creator working on a laptop", width: 525, height: 524, class: "h-auto w-full max-w-md" %>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="px-8 py-16 lg:px-16 lg:py-24" aria-labelledby="capabilities-title">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl">
      <div class="mb-12 max-w-3xl space-y-6">
        <p class="text-xl">An MCP server for selling digital products</p>
        <h2 id="capabilities-title" class="text-4xl font-medium text-balance md:text-6xl">What can you do with it?</h2>
        <p class="text-lg">Model Context Protocol (MCP) lets your AI assistant work with your store. Manage ebooks, templates, courses, and other digital products without leaving the chat.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid gap-10 md:grid-cols-3">
        <article class="space-y-5">
          <div class="flex h-56 items-center justify-center rounded-xl border border-black bg-yellow p-8">
            <%= image_tag "features/sales-graph.svg", alt: "", class: "h-full w-full object-contain", loading: "lazy" %>
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-medium">“Show my recent sales.”</h3>
          <p class="text-lg">See which products people bought and what they paid.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="space-y-5">
          <div class="flex h-56 items-center justify-center rounded-xl border border-black bg-pink p-8">
            <%= image_tag "features/books-and-writing.svg", alt: "", class: "h-full w-full object-contain", loading: "lazy" %>
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-medium">“Draft my next product.”</h3>
          <p class="text-lg">Ask for a product name, price, and description. Add the product files in Gumroad before publishing.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="space-y-5">
          <div class="flex h-56 items-center justify-center rounded-xl border border-black bg-purple p-8">
            <%= image_tag "about/coin-5.svg", alt: "", class: "h-full w-full object-contain", loading: "lazy" %>
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-medium">“Check my latest payouts.”</h3>
          <p class="text-lg">Check recent payout amounts and their status.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-y border-black px-8 py-16 lg:px-16 lg:py-24" aria-labelledby="clients-title">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl">
      <div class="mb-12 max-w-3xl space-y-6">
        <p class="text-xl">Choose your assistant</p>
        <h2 id="clients-title" class="text-4xl font-medium text-balance md:text-6xl">Which assistant can I connect?</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="grid gap-10 md:grid-cols-3">
        <% McpConnectorsController::CLIENTS.each do |key, client| %>
          <article class="flex flex-col justify-between gap-6 rounded-xl border border-black p-8">
            <div class="space-y-4">
              <h3 class="text-2xl font-medium">Gumroad MCP for <%= client[:label] %></h3>
              <% if client[:pending_review] %>
                <p class="text-lg">Submitted for review. The Gumroad connector is not yet available in <%= client[:label] %>.</p>
              <% else %>
                <p class="text-lg">Available now as a custom connector.</p>
                <% if client[:listing_notice] %>
                  <p class="text-base"><%= client[:listing_notice] %></p>
                <% end %>
              <% end %>
            </div>
            <%= link_to client[:pending_review] ? "Read the technical details" : "Set up Gumroad MCP", "/#{key}", class: "inline-flex min-h-11 items-center underline underline-offset-4" %>
          </article>
        <% end %>
        <article class="flex flex-col justify-between gap-6 rounded-xl border border-black p-8">
          <div class="space-y-4">
            <h3 class="text-2xl font-medium">ChatGPT</h3>
            <p class="text-lg">Not available yet. We’ll announce it here when the Gumroad connector is ready in ChatGPT.</p>
          </div>
          <%= link_to "Setup guide", McpConnectorsController::SETUP_GUIDE_URL, class: "inline-flex min-h-11 items-center underline underline-offset-4" %>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-10 max-w-3xl text-lg">Every assistant connects to its own URL and asks for OAuth access to your Gumroad account. Each connector page lists the exact address to paste.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="connect" class="scroll-mt-28 bg-dark-gray px-8 py-16 text-white lg:px-16 lg:py-24" aria-labelledby="connect-title">
    <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-7xl gap-12 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:gap-20">
      <div class="space-y-6">
        <p class="text-xl text-pink">Set up Gumroad MCP</p>
        <h2 id="connect-title" class="text-4xl font-medium text-balance md:text-6xl">How do you connect?</h2>
        <p class="max-w-xl text-lg">Setup takes three steps in the assistant you use. You stay signed in to Gumroad, and you can revoke access whenever you want.</p>
      </div>
      <ol class="list-none space-y-8 pl-0">
        <li class="space-y-3">
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-medium">1. Add the connector</h3>
          <p class="text-lg">Open your assistant’s connector settings and add a remote MCP server using the URL from its connector page.</p>
          <%= link_to "Gumroad MCP for Claude connector page", "/claude", class: "block text-lg underline underline-offset-4" %>
        </li>
        <li class="space-y-3">
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-medium">2. Connect your Gumroad account</h3>
          <p class="text-lg">Sign in to Gumroad when prompted. Review the requested permissions before you authorize access.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="space-y-3">
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-medium">3. Start a conversation</h3>
          <p class="text-lg">Select the connector in your chat. Try asking, “Show my Gumroad products.”</p>
        </li>
        <li class="space-y-3">
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-medium">Full step-by-step guide</h3>
          <p class="text-lg">The help center covers the permissions you grant, revoking access, and what to do when publishing fails.</p>
          <%= link_to "Connecting AI assistants to your Gumroad store", McpConnectorsController::SETUP_GUIDE_URL, class: "block text-lg underline underline-offset-4" %>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="px-8 py-16 lg:px-16 lg:py-24" aria-labelledby="access-title">
    <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-7xl gap-12 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:gap-20">
      <h2 id="access-title" class="text-4xl font-medium text-balance md:text-6xl">What access do you give your assistant?</h2>
      <div class="space-y-8 text-lg">
        <div class="space-y-3">
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-medium">What data can it read?</h3>
          <p>Your products, sales, buyer emails, and payouts, according to the permissions you grant. You can grant some and not others.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-medium">Can it publish products?</h3>
          <p>New products start as unpublished drafts. With product access, the connector can publish or unpublish them. Review these actions in your MCP client.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-medium">How do customers buy?</h3>
          <p>Share your product’s Gumroad link. Customers pay through Gumroad checkout. The MCP server does not take payments in your chat.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-medium">How do I revoke access?</h3>
          <p>Revoke the connection any time under <%= link_to "Authorized Applications", settings_authorized_applications_path %> in your Gumroad settings. Disconnecting the connector in your chat app does not revoke its access token, so revoke it here to end the connection.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="border-t border-black dark:border-white/35 px-8 py-10 lg:px-16">
    <div class="mx-auto flex max-w-7xl flex-col justify-between gap-6 md:flex-row">
      <nav aria-label="Connector details" class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-6 gap-y-2">
        <span>Connector details</span>
        <% McpConnectorsController::CLIENTS.each do |key, client| %>
          <%= link_to "Gumroad MCP for #{client[:label]}", "/#{key}", class: "inline-flex min-h-11 items-center underline underline-offset-4" %>
        <% end %>
      </nav>
      <nav aria-label="Developer resources" class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-6">
        <%= link_to "Setup guide", McpConnectorsController::SETUP_GUIDE_URL, class: "inline-flex min-h-11 items-center underline underline-offset-4" %>
        <%= link_to "API docs", "/api", class: "inline-flex min-h-11 items-center underline underline-offset-4" %>
        <%= link_to "MCP discovery", "/.well-known/mcp.json", class: "inline-flex min-h-11 items-center underline underline-offset-4" %>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </div>
  <%= render "home/shared/footer" %>
</div>
